IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 4 and 5 -- APPLYING, AND
-- THE DAY AN APPLICATION IS DEEMED APPROVED.
--
-- Section 4(1) (an application must be made in the form and manner the Minister specifies)
-- is not encoded: the Minister's specification is not in the text, so there is nothing
-- here to test; it is inert (NOTES.md, coverage).
--
-- "Month arithmetic" in this module uses `add months`, which clamps to the end of a short
-- month (31 August less six months is 28 February).

§ `Regulations s 4 -- Application for benefits`

-- 4(2) and 4(3): an application is made only when the Minister receives it, and one that
-- is received within the six months before the applicant's 18th birthday is deemed received
-- on that birthday. "Within six months before the day" is read as the period from the day
-- six months before the birthday up to the day before it, both ends included (fork F14).
-- NOTHING is returned for an application the Minister has not received.
-- src:66 | (2) An application is deemed to have been made only when it is received by the Minister.
-- src:67 | Application before 18th birthday
-- src:68 | (3) An application that is received by the Minister within six months before the day on which the applicant turns 18 years of age is deemed to have been received on that day.
@ref Regulations s 4(2) and (3) (src:66-68)
GIVEN `the day the Minister received the application` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an application is deemed to have been made` `the day the Minister received the application` `date of birth` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Minister received the application`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST received THEN
        JUST (IF     received AT LEAST `add months` eighteenth (0 MINUS 6)
                 AND received LESS THAN eighteenth
              THEN eighteenth
              ELSE received)
    WHERE eighteenth MEANS `add years` `date of birth` 18

-- 4(4): a beneficiary who becomes ineligible for a month stops receiving the allocation
-- as of that month and has to apply again. A month that is ineligible only because of a
-- suspension the beneficiary asked for (s 2(6)) is left out: s 11(3) to (5) govern what
-- happens then (fork F11).
-- src:70 | (4) If, for any given month, a beneficiary becomes ineligible to receive an allocation, the allocation ceases as of that month and they must make a new application for benefits to receive the allocation again.
@ref Regulations s 4(4) (src:70)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `Person facts for a month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` `the person is a beneficiary` facts MEANS
        `the person is a beneficiary`
    AND NOT `the person meets the criteria of section 2 apart from the bar in subsection 2(6)` facts

§ `Regulations s 5 -- Approval date`

-- 5(1) and 5(2): an application is deemed approved on the earliest day on which the
-- applicant becomes eligible and for which no benefit has been paid, but not earlier than
-- 24 months before the day the application is made. The earliest eligible day is asked
-- as a date (fork F13: the first day of the earliest month for which the applicant met
-- the criteria of section 2 and for which no benefit has been paid, because eligibility
-- is month by month). NOTHING when there is no such day.
-- src:72 | 5 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an application is deemed to be approved by the Minister on the earliest day on which an applicant becomes eligible for a benefit in accordance with the Act and these Regulations and for which a benefit has not already been paid.
-- src:73 | Time limit
-- src:74 | (2) The earliest day on which an application can be deemed to have been approved is the day that is 24 months before the day on which the application is made.
@ref Regulations s 5(1) and (2) (src:72-74)
GIVEN `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the earliest day on which the applicant becomes eligible for a benefit and for which no benefit has been paid` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an application is deemed to have been approved` `the day the application is made` `the earliest day on which the applicant becomes eligible for a benefit and for which no benefit has been paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earliest day on which the applicant becomes eligible for a benefit and for which no benefit has been paid`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST earliest THEN
        JUST (`the later day of` earliest (`add months` `the day the application is made` (0 MINUS 24)))
